Z||000003||skitime||09-04-2001||10:12 AM||||Nice car!  Where is Hellertown, PA? <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Springtyme||09-04-2001||11:00 AM||||Near Bethlehem, Allentown, Quakertown area. It's also close to Easton. If you know where I78 is, Hellertown is the second last exit before you leave the state and enter NJ.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||3
Z||000005||skitime||09-04-2001||11:24 AM||||Well you don't live very far from us.  We have an large active group of Fiero enthusiasts in the Lancaster/Reading area.  We often get together for shows, BBQs and tech sessions.  You should join us.  Many of us are going to be at the KSC Pontiac Fall Show in Reading on the 23rd. You should bring your car and show it. We are having a tech session in Reading in October too.  Make plans!<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever3000||09-04-2001||11:26 AM||||That's great.  It's a beautiful car.  Look at that, the console/radio area isn't warped!  Must have been garaged most of the time, so it's amazing you were able to notice it when you did.  Good find!  Good pics, too. ||||reg||1
